Description: Fix CVE-2026-55999 heap-buffer-overflow via PCF fonts with malicious per-glyph metrics
 A crafted PCF font can present per-glyph metrics that violate the font's
 maxbounds invariant, or that are negative. glamor_font_get() sizes its
 texture atlas slots from maxbounds but copies each glyph using
 GLYPHHEIGHTPIXELS/GLYPHWIDTHBYTES from the per-glyph data, producing an
 out-of-bounds heap write. The same signed INT16 metrics make
 `if (width && height)` true for negative dimensions in the fb, mi, and
 glamor glyph blitters, which then pass a negative height into loops that
 write out of bounds.
 .
 Backport for xorg-server 1.20.11 (Debian 11, 2:1.20.11-1+deb11u17).
 Debian's bullseye-security diff through 1.20.11-1+deb11u18 does not modify
 these four files, and the hunks apply to the 1.20.11 orig sources with no
 offset. Two upstream commits:
   * fbf7bac22e2c6bd627fb042742a23318263edae1
     Reject a non-positive atlas slot, and reject any glyph whose per-glyph
     metrics are negative or larger than that slot. Free the texture and
     the atlas buffer before returning NULL so glamor falls back to
     software rendering (miPolyText / miImageText). The memcpy loop then
     uses the checked signed width and height.
   * e31efd3e106e53bfc29d499ff0a34b0d20013f2d
     Require width > 0 and height > 0 in fbPolyGlyphBlt, fbImageGlyphBlt,
     glamor_poly_glyph_blt_gl, and miPolyGlyphBlt. Positive glyphs are
     unchanged; zero-size glyphs were already skipped.
 .
 test/pyxtest/ does not exist in 1.20.11, so those hunks are omitted.
